WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:16.530
On Monday Daisy walked to school with Kaleem.

2
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.351
Beatrice flew along with them.

3
00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:28.334
When they reached the building, Beatrice looked nervous.

4
00:00:28.354 --> 00:00:32.236
"I don't think I should go inside," she said.

5
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.301
"Too many people."

6
00:00:38.203 --> 00:00:39.024
Daisy nodded.

7
00:00:39.044 --> 00:00:42.787
"Why don't you stay outside until school ends?"

8
00:00:42.807 --> 00:00:44.608
"See you later!"

9
00:00:46.089 --> 00:00:47.310
Beatrice zipped off.

10
00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:56.276
Daisy was surprised to see her classmates in the hallway outside their classroom.

11
00:01:02.544 --> 00:01:04.765
"Good morning, students," their teacher said.

12
00:01:04.785 --> 00:01:06.566
"I have a surprise."

13
00:01:06.586 --> 00:01:09.228
"Did you outlaw homework?"

14
00:01:09.628 --> 00:01:10.548
Parker asked.

15
00:01:11.609 --> 00:01:12.790
Mr. Neal chuckled.

16
00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.332
"Nope. We have new class pets!"

17
00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:20.414
He flung open the door.

18
00:01:22.835 --> 00:01:27.638
From inside the room, Daisy heard dozens of tiny, chirping voices.

19
00:01:27.658 --> 00:01:29.138
"What's going on?"

20
00:01:29.158 --> 00:01:31.820
"This place is too small!"

21
00:01:32.496 --> 00:01:33.717
"Let us out!"

22
00:01:33.897 --> 00:01:35.758
"Oh no!"

23
00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:36.959
Daisy thought.

24
00:01:36.979 --> 00:01:39.481
"Those poor crickets!"

25
00:01:40.802 --> 00:01:43.864
The students rushed over to the glass tank of crickets.

26
00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:49.628
be interesting to observe them," Mr.

27
00:01:49.688 --> 00:01:50.248
Neal said.

28
00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:52.309
Daisy shook her head.

29
00:01:52.329 --> 00:01:54.371
"The crickets are awake now.

30
00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:56.812
But crickets are mostly nocturnal.

31
00:01:57.613 --> 00:02:00.515
They probably won't be very interesting to watch during the day."

32
00:02:00.535 --> 00:02:07.064
"So?" Parker tapped on the tank.

33
00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:10.065
"We'll keep them awake."

34
00:02:11.686 --> 00:02:12.646
Daisy frowned.

35
00:02:12.666 --> 00:02:14.246
"That's mean!"

36
00:02:15.607 --> 00:02:16.947
Parker rolled his eyes.

37
00:02:16.967 --> 00:02:21.208
"Only a birdbrain like you cares about being nice to bugs."

38
00:02:21.228 --> 00:02:24.949
"Don't insult your classmate, Parker," Mr.

39
00:02:25.009 --> 00:02:26.110
Neal said sharply.

40
00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.370
"And don't worry, Daisy.

41
00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:29.811
The crickets will be fine."

42
00:02:29.831 --> 00:02:32.871
"But they won't be fine," Daisy said.

43
00:02:32.891 --> 00:02:34.672
"Maybe we should let them out."

44
00:02:35.252 --> 00:02:37.013
"What? No!"

45
00:02:37.573 --> 00:02:39.713
Raj, Parker's best friend, said.

46
00:02:39.733 --> 00:02:42.994
"We haven't had a class pet all year.

47
00:02:43.774 --> 00:02:45.575
And I thought you liked animals."

48
00:02:45.595 --> 00:02:48.496
"I do," Daisy said.

49
00:02:48.516 --> 00:02:50.476
"We could get a different pet.

50
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:55.878
Maybe fish, or another animal that doesn't mind being trapped in a small space."

51
00:02:57.098 --> 00:02:58.559
"Sit down, kids," Mr.

52
00:02:58.619 --> 00:02:59.219
Neal said.

53
00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:01.199
"It's time to start class."

54
00:03:03.888 --> 00:03:06.370
All morning Daisy had trouble concentrating.

55
00:03:07.051 --> 00:03:09.373
The crickets talked nonstop.

56
00:03:10.554 --> 00:03:11.975
"This place is too crowded!"

57
00:03:11.995 --> 00:03:15.358
"Let's escape!"

58
00:03:15.378 --> 00:03:17.620
"I don't like it here."

59
00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:23.104
Finally it was time for recess.

60
00:03:25.026 --> 00:03:27.748
On her way out, Daisy stopped by the tank.

61
00:03:27.768 --> 00:03:32.092
"Sorry, crickets," she whispered.

62
00:03:32.616 --> 00:03:33.677
"I'll try to fix this."

63
00:03:33.697 --> 00:03:35.237
"Thank you!"

64
00:03:35.637 --> 00:03:37.218
the crickets chirped loudly.

65
00:03:39.199 --> 00:03:41.140
Kaleem was digging through his desk.

66
00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.901
Daisy was going to wait for him.

67
00:03:44.661 --> 00:03:47.202
But then she noticed Grace heading outside.

68
00:03:48.843 --> 00:03:50.023
She ran to catch up.

69
00:03:50.043 --> 00:03:52.944
"Have you heard how Mrs.

70
00:03:53.024 --> 00:03:53.965
Ortiz is doing?"

71
00:03:54.385 --> 00:03:55.185
Daisy asked.

72
00:03:56.026 --> 00:03:57.166
Grace shook her head.

73
00:03:57.186 --> 00:04:01.628
"After we walked Scamp last night, my mom called to check on her.

74
00:04:02.512 --> 00:04:04.093
She's still in the hospital.

75
00:04:04.754 --> 00:04:07.836
She asked if we could take care of Scamp for a few more days.

76
00:04:08.637 --> 00:04:09.638
Is that okay?"

77
00:04:09.658 --> 00:04:12.680
"Of course," Daisy said.

78
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.362
"It's hot today.

79
00:04:15.122 --> 00:04:17.484
We should make sure his pool is full of water."

80
00:04:18.525 --> 00:04:19.306
Grace nodded.

81
00:04:19.326 --> 00:04:21.167
"My dad works from home.

82
00:04:22.148 --> 00:04:23.909
He's going to walk him at lunchtime.

83
00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.111
We can check on him after school."

84
00:04:26.852 --> 00:04:27.972
Kaleem hurried over.

85
00:04:27.992 --> 00:04:30.675
"Want to play soccer?

86
00:04:31.415 --> 00:04:34.441
But watch out—I learned a new way to juggle the ball!"

87
00:04:42.063 --> 00:04:45.063
The three of them played soccer until recess was over.

88
00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:49.685
Then they went inside with the rest of the class.

89
00:04:55.406 --> 00:04:57.627
When they got there, Daisy gasped.

90
00:04:59.047 --> 00:05:01.448
The glass tank was lying on its side.

91
00:05:02.857 --> 00:05:04.060
"Oh no!"

92
00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.083
Grace whispered.

93
00:05:05.103 --> 00:05:07.589
"The crickets are loose!"
